# RULE 36 — CLAUDE SERIAL SHIP SEQUENCE (owner law — permanent)

**Owner word (2026-08-05):** Claude stays mergeable (~1/10 issues, 50+ PRs without rebase thrash). Cursor was 1/1 fail + hours of rebase. Inspect Claude’s method. Implement it. Make it the permanent Cursor sequence.

## Why Claude stays green (measured)

| Claude does | Cursor was doing (defect) |
|-------------|---------------------------|
| **One** money/CLAIMED-touching PR at a time; next only after merge | 2–N parallel EntityPicker PRs all editing `CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json` → perpetual CONFLICTING |
| Branch tip = **exactly** `origin/main` + **one** FINDING commit | Stacked / stale base / wrong tip force-push (e.g. #4369 tip overwritten with #4366 squash) |
| Title: `Claude-1- fix(module): FINDING — one-line defect` | `Cursor- fix: short name` (no module, no FINDING, no defect sentence) |
| Body = FINDING-first prose ROOT CAUSE (measured) + FIX + GUARD + LIVE PROOF artifact | `## Summary` / “Made with Cursor” / `DRAFT — WIP` / weak UNVERIFIED |
| Local gate PASS → **one** push → stop | Push → watch CI → fix → rebase → repeat (3 hours) |
| Sibling guards updated **in the same commit** as pattern migrations | New guard only → sibling Combobox asserts still red |

## HARD SEQUENCE (every Cursor PR — no shortcuts)

Run in order. Skipping a step is a trust defect.

```text
0) WIP — count open non-Dependabot feature PRs. If ≥3, finish/park before opening another
   (P0 main-unblock exempt). Cursor CLAIMED/verify-step PRs: MAX 1 open at a time.

1) git fetch origin main
   git checkout -B cursor/<slug> origin/main
   # NEVER branch from another open feature tip. NEVER reuse a polluted remote tip.

2) Build ONE ranked FAIL:
   code + every sibling guard that names the touched file + new guard + CLAIMED-REGEN
   (union claimed dict; never drop main's keys)

3) Write /tmp/pr-body.txt from docs/templates/CLAUDE-GREEN-PR-BODY.md
   - column-0 FINDING:
   - no ## Summary first, no "Made with Cursor", no "DRAFT — WIP" in body

4) Title (Claude shape):
   Cursor- fix(<module>): <FINDING-ID> — <one-line defect>
   Example: Cursor- fix(insurance): INS-CLAIM-LOAD-TRAILER-PICKER — ClaimCreate still Combobox+listLoads

5) Commit ONCE with the same labelled block as the PR body (Rule 30).

6) node scripts/ops/cursor-ship-preflight.mjs --body-file /tmp/pr-body.txt
   → must PASS (includes tip-contains-origin/main check)

7) IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSH (mandatory — this is why Claude never rebases for hours):
   git fetch origin main
   git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main HEAD || git rebase origin/main
   # if rebase ran: re-run step 6

8) ONE push (hooks ON). Prefer --force-with-lease only after a tip-main rebase.
   gh pr create --body-file /tmp/pr-body.txt   # READY — never draft for finished work

9) Do NOT open a second CLAIMED/verify-step PR until this one is squash-merged
   (or closed with feature preserved). Serialize Claimed thrash = zero.

10) If main advances and GitHub shows CONFLICTING / behind≥1:
    same turn: fetch → rebase → preflight → force-with-lease.
    Never leave CONFLICTING overnight. Never "babysit then rebase later."
```

## Forbidden forever

- Parallel Cursor PRs that both edit `scripts/verify-steps/CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json`
- Opening feature PRs that add `verify-steps/NNNN-*.mjs` before `NNNN` is on `origin/main` (Rule 37)
- Combining claim + guard on `chore/claim-reserve-*` (claim-only vs feature — two PRs)
- Force-pushing an unrelated squash/merge SHA onto a feature branch tip
- `git reset --soft origin/main` (Rule 30 — deletes other guards)
- Opening draft “for WIP accounting” when the work is finished
- Pushing without `cursor-ship-preflight --body-file`
- Starting the next CLAIMED/verify-step PR before the current one merges
- Per-site EntityPicker / identical-codemod PRs when ≥3 sites share one transform (§9.0 item **17** — ONE sweep + ONE generalized guard)

